@startuml launcher-sequence
' UML sequence diagram only: participants, lifelines, sync and async messages,
' replies and notes, and no other diagram or UML element type. The subject is
' the transport contract `run` actually gets: the base image's PID 1 chain.
' Source of record for docs/diagrams/launcher-sequence.svg. Do not edit the SVG:
' render it with the pinned PlantUML image (docs/adopting.md).
' &#45;&#45; is a literal "--": PlantUML reads --text-- as strikeout.
title run transport: pipes, signals and exit code through the image's PID 1

participant "host harness" as H
participant "agentjail\nrun" as C
participant "podman\n(client, then conmon)" as P
participant "container PID 1\ntini" as T
participant "agent\n(child of tini,\nexec'd by agentjail-entrypoint)" as A

H -> C : start agentjail run with fd 0/1/2 attached,\nand wait for it to exit
H ->> C : stdin (JSON-RPC frames)
C -> P : podman run &#45;&#45;rm &#45;&#45;interactive,\nfd 0/1/2 are pipes, not a TTY
P -> T : start the container's PID 1 and wait
T -> A : spawn the agent (the entrypoint exec'd it) and wait
P ->> T : the same bytes on the container's fd 0
T ->> A : inherited fd 0
A ->> T : stdout
T ->> P : stdout, never mixed with stderr
P ->> C : stdout
C ->> H : stdout
A ->> T : stderr
T ->> P : stderr, a separate stream
P ->> C : stderr
C ->> H : stderr
H ->> C : SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGQUIT
C ->> P : forward each one unchanged\n(supervising; exec'd when nothing needs cleanup)
P ->> T : deliver to the container's PID 1
T ->> A : forward to its only child
A --> T : exit code 42
T --> P : exit code 42
P --> C : exit code 42
C --> H : exit code 42, or 128 + N when the agent died from signal N
note over T, A : tini reaps orphans and forwards to its direct child only, so the\nagent's own grandchildren are not signalled; no TTY is in this path
note over H, A
  agentjail-launcher is not in this path. images/base/Containerfile sets
  ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/bin/tini", "&#45;&#45;", "/usr/local/bin/agentjail-entrypoint"]
  and the entrypoint execs the agent, so tini is PID 1. Only an image whose
  entrypoint execs the launcher reaches the launcher's own contract: refuse
  root, exec the agent in its own process group, forward
  SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGQUIT/SIGWINCH to that group, and exit with the agent's code
  (128 + N for signal N).
  Synchronous calls (->) carry their reply (-->); the bare ->> arrows are
  asynchronous by design: the three fd streams are bytes written without
  waiting, and a signal is a notification, not a call.
end note
@enduml
